{"agents":[{"agent_name":"/root","agent_status":"running"},{"agent_name":"/root/flow_recon","agent_status":{"completed":"The create and reply controllers are the right lock boundary. Acquire a synchronous actor lock before calling `api.topics.create` or `api.topics.reply`, and release it in `finally` after the awaited operation. Use `req.uid` for authenticated users and `req.sessionID` for guests.

The existing API wrapper converts a thrown error to HTTP 400 with `status.code: "bad-request"`; a normal create response is HTTP 200 with `status.code: "ok"`. Topic and post counters are updated within the awaited create path, so holding the lock through that call covers those writes.

For regression coverage, use a shared authenticated session, submit the minimal `{ cid, title, content }` payload concurrently, and compare topic and post counts before and after. The existing `helpers.request` fetches CSRF tokens separately per call, which can stagger requests; fetching one token before launching the burst gives a clearer overlap test. I made no edits or ran tests; this was a read-only investigation delegated by the root agent."}},{"agent_name":"/root/patch_review","agent_status":{"completed":"Review complete. The lock correctly rejects overlapping requests within one worker, releases on success or failure, and maps rejection to HTTP 400 with `status.code: "bad-request"`. The remaining limitation is that its in-memory `Set` does not coordinate across NodeBB workers. Prefixing user and session keys would also avoid identity collisions. I made no edits or test runs."}},{"agent_name":"/root/regression_test","agent_status":{"completed":"Added the concurrent creation regression test in [test/topics.js](/app/test/topics.js:173). It checks response codes, the single topic created, counter updates, and lock release on a later request. ESLint passed. Mocha was left for the coordinator to run without database overlap."}}]}
